<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no" ?>
<FinalDraft DocumentType="Script" Template="No" Version="5">

  <Content>
    <Paragraph Type="New Act">
      <Text>Chapter 1: awakening</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 3/8" Page="1" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="FOX-BOY">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="GHOST">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. SLEEPING VOID</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Shot">
      <Text>SHOT: WIDE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>FOX-BOY sleeps an dreamless slumber, nothing around, nothing but the white void. He’s serene. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Shot">
      <Text>SHOT: DIRECT FACE, above HEAD</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>He awakes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>FOX-BOY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Where... am I?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A creature appears, it’s black with eyes red, ghostly tendrils, and the facade of something once was.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The ghost has a voice of power, it speaks not like any ghost from movies. The ghost might speak in cryptic ways, but it’s truly sapient.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>GHOST</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(slowly)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Who are you?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>FOX-BOY is thrown off.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>FOX-BOY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I- I’m a fox.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>GHOST</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>That is what matter you are composed of.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>FOX-BOY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Well, I’m FOX-BOY.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>GHOST</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>That is only a name.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The void is unsettling to the fox, something familiar, but not entirely comforting.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>GHOST</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Who are you?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>FOX-BOY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I am-</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"/>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>GHOST</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Who are you?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>FOX-BOY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I-</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>GHOST</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(intense)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Who are you?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>FOX-BOY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I don’t know.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A tear.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The space settles. The ghost isn’t happy with that answer. It’ll have to do for now.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="4/8" Page="2" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="FOX-BOY">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. FOX-BOY’s home - morning</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Shot">
      <Text>CUT: MATCH CUT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>FOX-BOY lays in bed asleep, tearing up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>And... He awakes in heavy breaths.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"/>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>FOX-BOY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>What am I?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>He looks at his hand-paws.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The room is a mess, items everywhere, there’s no structure or thought to the placement of anything.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>He get’s up, get’s dressed and leaves his house.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="1/8" Page="2" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. VILLAGE - MORNING</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>There is a freshness to this day, perhaps it’s attributed to the spring weather, but it certainly is a nice day.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"/>
  </Content>

